{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8282e01a424d038d","name":"card_event_run_the_battlefield","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BloodIron/events/card_event_run_the_battlefield","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RUN THE BATTLEFIELD","text":"For each of your units with 4 or more attack, randomly gain 3 kredits, give it +2+2 or draw a card.","flavorText":"Overall, German generals were often characterized by their aggressiveness, adaptability and frontline presence, which contrasted with the more methodical, organized, and often remote command styles of Allied generals. This approach contributed to early German successes but also led to high casualty rates among German leadership as the war progressed. Notable examples include commanders like Erwin Rommel and Walter Model, who frequently exposed themselves to enemy fire to rally their troops and strengthen defenses. This hands-on leadership style not only boosted soldier morale but also allowed these generals to make rapid, situational adjustments. However, it placed them in greater personal danger and resulted in irreplaceable losses within the German command structure as the war wore on.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_run_the_battlefield","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_run_the_battlefield_title","SourceString":"RUN THE BATTLEFIELD","LocalizedString":"RUN THE BATTLEFIELD"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_run_the_battlefield_text","SourceString":"For each of your units with 4 or more attack, randomly gain 3 kredits, give it +2+2 or draw a card.","LocalizedString":"For each of your units with 4 or more attack, randomly gain 3 kredits, give it +2+2 or draw a card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_run_the_battlefield_histo